# Caching rules for the live site, read by Netlify and by Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The page and its code are checked with the server on every visit — a quick
# "has this changed?" that answers "no" almost always, so the site stays fast
# but an update reaches visitors straight away. Without this, a browser can
# hold on to an old style.css while loading a new script.js and render a
# half-updated page. That is not hypothetical: it happened during development
# and cost an afternoon of chasing a bug that was never in the code.
#
# Artwork keeps its name from one deploy to the next but changes rarely, so it
# is cached for a week to keep the gallery quick.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
